  "description": "The KANGDUO SR2000 is a modular teleoperated surgical robotic system developed by Harbin Sagebot Intelligent Medical Equipment Co., Ltd. (Sagebot). Built for multiport robot-assisted minimally invasive surgery (RAMIS), the platform consists of a single patient cart featuring four multi-joint robotic arms, an ergonomic open surgeon console with an high-definition 3D stereoscopic display viewed via passive polarized glasses, and a mobile vision cart housing the 3D endoscopic imaging processor and illumination system. The SR2000 received NMPA marketing approval in China in 2024 and European CE mark certification, with clinical indications covering urological, gynecological, general abdominal, and thoracic procedures.",
